 "deepseek_ch1_p35": "<section data-page=\"35\">\n<h2>Section 1.2 Domain and Range</h2>\n<p>Write a formula for the piecewise function graphed below.</p>\n<figure>\n<figcaption>Graph 25: A piecewise graph with a horizontal segment at \\(y=2\\) from \\(x=-6\\) to \\(x=0\\) (solid endpoints), a horizontal segment at \\(y=-2\\) from \\(x=0\\) (open) to \\(x=2\\) (solid), and a horizontal segment at \\(y=-4\\) from \\(x=2\\) (open) to \\(x=4\\) (solid).</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>25.</p>\n<figure>\n<figcaption>Graph 26: A piecewise graph with a horizontal segment at \\(y=5\\) from \\(x=-1\\) (open) to \\(x=1\\) (solid), a horizontal segment at \\(y=-3\\) from \\(x=-6\\) to \\(x=-2\\) (solid endpoints), and a horizontal segment at \\(y=-3\\) from \\(x=1\\) (open) to \\(x=5\\) (solid).</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>26.</p>\n<figure>\n<figcaption>Graph 27: A graph with a horizontal ray at \\(y=3\\) extending left from \\(x=0\\) (solid), and a curve increasing from the open point \\((0,0)\\) upward to the right.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>27.</p>\n<figure>\n<figcaption>Graph 28: A graph with a line decreasing from the left to the point \\((0,0)\\), then increasing to the point \\((2,2)\\) (solid), and a horizontal ray at \\(y=3\\) extending right from \\(x=2\\) (open).</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>28.</p>\n<figure>\n<figcaption>Graph 29: A graph with a horizontal ray at \\(y=0\\) extending left from \\(x=0\\) (open), and a curve increasing from the open point \\((0,0)\\) to the right.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>29.</p>\n<figure>\n<figcaption>Graph 30: A graph with a horizontal ray at \\(y=-1\\) extending left from \\(x=0\\) (solid), a curve rising from \\((0,-1)\\) to \\((1,1)\\) (open), and a horizontal ray at \\(y=2\\) extending right from \\(x=1\\) (solid).</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>30.</p>\n<p>Sketch a graph of each piecewise function</p>\n<table class=\"equation-table\">\n<tr>\n<td>31. \\(f(x) = \\begin{cases} |x| & \\text{if } x < 2 \\\\ 5 & \\text{if } x \\ge 2 \\end{cases}\\)</td>\n<td>32. \\(f(x) = \\begin{cases} 4 & \\text{if } x < 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{x} & \\text{if } x \\ge 0 \\end{cases}\\)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33. \\(f(x) = \\begin{cases} x^2 & \\text{if } x < 0 \\\\ x+2 & \\text{if } x \\ge 0 \\end{cases}\\)</td>\n<td>34. \\(f(x) = \\begin{cases} x+1 & \\text{if } x < 1 \\\\ x^3 & \\text{if } x \\ge 1 \\end{cases}\\)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>35. \\(f(x) = \\begin{cases} 3 & \\text{if } x \\le -2 \\\\ -x+1 & \\text{if } -2 < x \\le 1 \\\\ 3 & \\text{if } x > 1 \\end{cases}\\)</td>\n<td>36. \\(f(x) = \\begin{cases} -3 & \\text{if } x \\le -2 \\\\ x-1 & \\text{if } -2 < x \\le 2 \\\\ 0 & \\text{if } x > 2 \\end{cases}\\)</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</section>",
 "deepseek_ch1_p35_run1": "<section data-page=\"35\">\n  <h2>Write a formula for the piecewise function graphed below.</h2>\n\n  <figure>\n    <figcaption><strong>25.</strong> Graph of a piecewise function with three horizontal segments: a closed segment from \\((-6,2)\\) to \\((-1,2)\\); a segment from \\((0,-2)\\) (open circle) to \\((2,-2)\\) (closed circle); and a segment from \\((2,-4)\\) (open circle) to \\((4,-4)\\) (closed circle).</figcaption>\n  </figure>\n\n  <figure>\n    <figcaption><strong>26.</strong> Graph of a piecewise function with three horizontal segments: a segment from \\((-1,5)\\) (open circle) to \\((1,5)\\) (closed circle); a segment from \\((0,-3)\\) (open circle) to \\((4,-3)\\) (closed circle); and a closed segment from \\((-6,-4)\\) to \\((-2,-4)\\).</figcaption>\n  </figure>\n\n  <figure>\n    <figcaption><strong>27.</strong> Graph of a piecewise function: a horizontal ray along \\(y=3\\) extending to the left from a closed circle at \\((0,3)\\), and a curve starting at an open circle at \\((0,0)\\) and rising to the right through \\((1,1)\\) to \\((2,4)\\) with an arrow.</figcaption>\n  </figure>\n\n  <figure>\n    <figcaption><strong>28.</strong> Graph of a piecewise function: a line from \\((-4,4)\\) down to \\((0,0)\\), continuing up to a closed circle at \\((2,2)\\), and a horizontal ray at \\(y=3\\) extending to the right from an open circle at \\((2,3)\\).</figcaption>\n  </figure>\n\n  <figure>\n    <figcaption><strong>29.</strong> Graph of a piecewise function: a horizontal ray along \\(y=0\\) extending to the left from an open circle at the origin; a curve descending from the origin along the \\(y\\)-axis to about \\((0,-5)\\) with an arrow; and a curve rising from the origin through \\((1,1)\\) and \\((4,2)\\) with an arrow.</figcaption>\n  </figure>\n\n  <figure>\n    <figcaption><strong>30.</strong> Graph of a piecewise function: a horizontal ray along \\(y=-1\\) extending to the left from a closed circle at \\((0,-1)\\); 